    "source": "M1 Lesson 1 · In-Content Questions",
    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<p>Which of the following will be reported under the items that will not be subsequently reclassified to profit or loss? Select ALL that apply.</p><ol class=\"answer-options\"><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">a)</span><span>Gain £15,000 from the revaluation of property</span></li><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">b)</span><span>Actuarial loss £5,000 related to defined benefit pension plans</span></li><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">c)</span><span>Gain £7,000 on exchange differences on retranslating year end trade receivables</span></li></ol>",
    "a": "<p class=\"answer-key\">The correct answers are a and b.</p><p>Gains on revaluation and remeasurements of defined benefit pension plans are amounts that will not be subsequently reclassified to profit or loss and are presented as such in the statement of other comprehensive income. Exchange differences on retranslating year end trade receivables is posted directly to profit or loss.</p>",
