    "lesson": "Lesson4",
    "source": "M1 Lesson 4 · In-Content Questions",
    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<p>Adjusting or non-adjusting event?</p><p>Select ALL the items on the following list that are adjusting events after the reporting period.</p><ol class=\"answer-options\"><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">a)</span><span>Receipt of information in respect to an impairment in the value of a long-term investment</span></li><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">b)</span><span>A court case settlement</span></li><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">c)</span><span>Announcement of a major restructuring</span></li><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">d)</span><span>A change in the valuation of inventories</span></li><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">e)</span><span>The declaration of a dividend</span></li><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">f)</span><span>Discovery of an error in the financial statements</span></li><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">g)</span><span>A major flood that damaged one of the warehouses</span></li><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">h)</span><span>The acquisition of a building that is a historic landmark with substantial value</span></li></ol>",
    "a": "<p class=\"answer-key\">The correct answers a, b, d and f.</p><p>Full details regarding each item would need to be obtained but items a, b, d, and f would normally be adjusting events and, therefore, a journal entry would be required to include the effect of the event within the financial statements. The remainder are normally non-adjusting. Disclosure of the non-adjusting events will depend on their significance.</p>",
