    "source": "M1 Lesson 5 · In-Content Questions",
    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<p>The following information relates to three separate divisions of a company. Each division is a component of the company, and each represents a separate line of business or a geographical area of operations. The year-end date of the company is 31 March 20X3.</p><p>Please provide your response on how each division should be accounted for in the financial statements of the company for the year ended 31 March 20X3.</p><p>Division A</p><p>This division has been in operation for several years. It was sold in November 20X2.</p><ol class=\"answer-options\"><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">a)</span><span>It should be treated as a discontinued operation.</span></li><li><span class=\"choice-letter\">b)</span><span>It should not be treated as a discontinued operation.</span></li></ol>",
    "a": "<p class=\"answer-key\">The correct answer is a.</p><p>This should be treated as a discontinued operation as it has been disposed of during the year. The other criteria are assumed to be met. The results up to the date of disposal should be classified as discontinued.</p>",
